{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791045549,"nonce":"16GtlsCPZDawICzazD7ax4yEHJk=","title":"Implicit abstract conversions are applied in too few places and matched by TypeId","message":"Rows: Issue9057, Issue10336, Issue2661, Issue9688 (plus Issue4100, Issue5385 in 4c1d8fb).\n- `@:to Bool` is not applied at if/while conditions or switch guards: `maybe_abstract_to_convert`\n  (ir/mir/helpers/stdlib.rs) runs only at var init, assignment and casts (Issue9057).\n- `@:from` rules are selected by exact `from_type == source_type`: generic parameters (`f:T-\u003eT`,\n  `Array\u003cT\u003e`), function types and structural types (`{x:Int,?y:Int}` against an object literal) never\n  match (Issue10336, Issue9688).\n- `@:to` to a non-primitive target (another abstract) is skipped by `coerce_arg_via_abstract_to`\n  (tast calls.rs) and `has_abstract_to_function` (Issue2661).\nA typer-level cast insertion against the expected type would cover all of them. Extends 4c1d8fb.","files":null}]}